**A soft 404 is a URL whose content says "missing" (or is effectively empty) while the HTTP status is 200 OK. Search engines try to detect these and typically treat them as errors, which pollutes reports and wastes crawl capacity.**

## How React apps create them

A classic single-page app is served by a catch-all rule: every path returns `index.html` with 200, and the client-side router decides what to render. For `/vehicles/not-a-model` the JS fetches data, receives an empty result and renders "Vehicle not found", but the server already said 200.

```tsx
// Anti-pattern: client-only check, server still answers 200
function VehiclePage({ slug }: { slug: string }) {
  const { data } = useVehicle(slug);
  if (!data) return <p>Vehicle not found</p>;
  return <h1>{data.name}</h1>;
}
```

## Fixes

- **Server-rendered frameworks**: do the lookup on the server and trigger the framework's not-found path.

```tsx
// Next.js App Router
import { notFound } from 'next/navigation';

export default async function Page({ params }: { params: Promise<{ slug: string }> }) {
  const { slug } = await params;
  const vehicle = await getVehicle(slug);
  if (!vehicle) notFound(); // renders not-found UI and 404 status
  return <h1>{vehicle.name}</h1>;
}
```

- **Pure SPA with no server logic**: configure the host or edge to return 404 for known-invalid patterns, or, as a last resort, add a `noindex` robots meta tag via JavaScript on the error view, or redirect to a real 404 URL. These are weaker than a true server status.
- **Removed content**: use 404 or 410 for permanent removal, or a 301 to a genuinely equivalent page.

## Other soft-404 sources

- Empty category or search-result pages with no items.
- Expired campaign pages left as "sorry, offer ended" with 200.
- Mass redirects of unrelated removed pages to the homepage.

## How to detect

Search Console reports "Soft 404"; also curl routes that should not exist and confirm the status, and crawl for pages with very low word count and an error phrase.

**In the Next.js App Router, each `layout.tsx` or `page.tsx` can export a static `metadata` object or an async `generateMetadata` function. Next.js renders those tags on the server and merges them down the route tree.**

```tsx
// app/[locale]/vehicles/[slug]/page.tsx
import type { Metadata } from 'next';
import { notFound } from 'next/navigation';

type Props = { params: Promise<{ locale: string; slug: string }> };

export async function generateMetadata({ params }: Props): Promise<Metadata> {
  const { locale, slug } = await params;
  const vehicle = await getVehicle(slug, locale); // shared, cached data fetch
  if (!vehicle) return { robots: { index: false } };

  const path = '/vehicles/' + slug;
  return {
    title: vehicle.seoTitle,
    description: vehicle.seoDescription,
    alternates: {
      canonical: '/' + locale + path,
      languages: { 'en-US': '/en-us' + path, 'en-GB': '/en-gb' + path },
    },
    openGraph: { title: vehicle.seoTitle, images: [vehicle.heroImageUrl] },
  };
}
```

## Notes

- Set `metadataBase` in the root layout so relative URLs resolve to absolute ones.
- Data fetches in the page and in `generateMetadata` with the same arguments are typically deduplicated by the framework's request memoization, but confirm for your data client; otherwise use a cached helper.
- Page-level metadata overrides layout metadata for the same field; plan defaults and overrides deliberately.
- Missing entities should call `notFound()` in the page so the status is 404; metadata alone does not set it.
- Add `robots: { index: false }` for utility, preview and filtered pages that should not be indexed.
- JSON-LD is not part of the metadata API; render it in the page as a script element.
- In the older Pages Router, use `next/head` and server-side data functions, and keep the tags in the server HTML.

## Verify

```bash
curl -s https://www.example.com/en-us/vehicles/explorer | grep -iE '<title|canonical|hreflang|robots'
```

## Common mistakes

Setting titles client-side with an effect, forgetting canonicals on dynamic routes, and letting preview deployments be indexed (use noindex or authentication there).
